    "purpose": "Use programs decomposed into space units with measurable requirements. This is the ADAPT layer: it is what a shell is tested against. A use program is deliberately NOT a layout — it is a demand profile, so the same shell can be scored against many programs without redrawing anything.",
    "provenance_policy": "Seeded values are 'indicative' working figures for model development. Verify each against BBR, SS 91 42 21, SS 25268, Boverket guidance, or municipal programme requirements (Stockholms stad) before publishing any result.",
    "verification_status": "UNVERIFIED — seeded for model development 2026-09-22",
    "binding_constraint_field": "Each space unit names its 'binding_constraint' — the requirement most likely to fail first in a reuse test. This is the field that makes the fit engine fast and the conversation with clients honest: you lead with what breaks, not with what fits."
  },

